      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, indeed.\n\nFor now we may just add a FIXME for this, plus maybe change the BUG_ON to returning -E2BIG or whatever?\n\nBriefly looking at pKVM-ARM, looks like it fixes host MMU page states in `fix_host_ownership()` _before_ unmapping anything from the host MMU in `unmap_protected_regions()` (so `fix_host_ownership()` doesn\u0027t need to deal with non-present entries), and then `unmap_protected_regions()` uses the memory protection API to unmap regions from the host MMU.",
