      "writtenOn": "2026-08-07T07:31:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eImplement the idea I described long ago in the comment in pkvm_host_use_dma(): initialize MMIO page states not with (PKVM_PAGE_NONE, PKVM_ID_HYP) but with (PKVM_PAGE_NONE, PKVM_ID_HOST) (which means simply leaving PTEs zeroed, i.e. do nothing), denoting that the given MMIO page is already owned by the host, not by the hypervisor, just hasn\u0027t been lazily mapped for the host yet. (That will also align it with pKVM-ARM which has the same assumption, for instance, in its lazy MMIO mapping in host_stage2_fault() -\u003e host_stage2_adjust_range -\u003e if (pte) return -EPERM.)\n\nI recalled you ever mentioned this idea. Then the host EPT violation handler needs to directly map MMIO in host mmu, rather than donating from the hyp. Seems this is also more friendly for the host to donate a MMIO page which is not mapped in the host MMU yet to a pVM.\n\n\u003eAfter that, fix the issue simply by using pkvm_pgtable_set_owner() instead of plain pkvm_pgtable_unmap() for unmapping pKVM and pvmfw memory from host MMU.\n\nYeah, so the `fix_host_mmu_pgstate` should be called before unmapping pKVM and pvmfw from host mmu.\n\nFor pvmfw memory, seems it doesn\u0027t have `struct pkvm_page`, it should be fine to use `pkvm_pgtable_set_owner` to unmap and set owner in PTEs.\n\nFor pKVM\u0027s memory, it has `struct pkvm_page`, and its state and owner are stored in `struct pkvm_page` rather than PTEs, so we can still use pkvm_pgtable_unmap() to unmap and then use set_host_mem_pgstate to fix the state/owner?\n\n\u003eI\u0027m gonna try to implement that.\n\nThanks. Then I will drop this patch.",
      "parentUuid": "0692c8e7_4b1dcd2a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 357,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 363,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "7f24bd9d05e623d2c8ece079f75cda4e8b8ff1ec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
