      "message": "BTW just a side note: pKVM-ARM takes a different approach: it forces adding pvmfw to the pKVM\u0027s memblock list even if pvmfw is not in the kernel\u0027s memory memblock (aosp/3864884), so that pKVM treats pvmfw as memory and thus doesn\u0027t need to special-case it like we are doing here.\n\nAlthough that is currently buggy (fix aosp/4217426 not merged yet), so maybe we shouldn\u0027t rush to adopt the same approach in pKVM-IA just yet.",
